WEBVTT

00:02:04.450 --> 00:02:13.660
Fight! Fight!

00:02:29.930 --> 00:02:31.470
What the heck is this?

00:02:31.850 --> 00:02:35.850
Okay! Those of you who aren't pilots
have leave to hit the showers now.

00:02:35.850 --> 00:02:37.980
However... pilots, give me another lap!

00:02:37.980 --> 00:02:39.850
- ﻿What?!
- Why?!

00:02:39.860 --> 00:02:41.440
Doctor, this is just cruel!

00:02:41.440 --> 00:02:44.150
Why are you making us sweat so hard?

00:02:44.740 --> 00:02:46.360
I can't take any more!

00:02:46.950 --> 00:02:50.410
How many days are you going to subject
us to this before you're satisfied?

00:02:50.410 --> 00:02:50.990
It helps with protecting against
cosmic radiation exposure

00:02:50.990 --> 00:02:52.870
Raraiya!

00:02:52.870 --> 00:02:55.830
and with expelling waste from the body.

00:03:01.090 --> 00:03:02.210
Good work, everyone.

00:03:04.800 --> 00:03:06.720
Darn it.

00:03:06.720 --> 00:03:08.550
I can still run!

00:03:08.550 --> 00:03:11.050
- Lorucca.
- I-I can keep going...

00:03:11.050 --> 00:03:12.300
Your legs are trembling.

00:03:12.850 --> 00:03:14.720
I'm not doing this to bully you.

00:03:14.720 --> 00:03:16.890
It's for when we enter the Venus Globe.

00:03:16.890 --> 00:03:19.020
- ﻿Dr. Flaminia.
- ﻿Yes.

00:03:20.860 --> 00:03:23.730
I can't believe she kept this
from me all this time.

00:03:23.730 --> 00:03:25.690
Time to hit the showers!

00:03:26.070 --> 00:03:29.530
None of them seem to carry
any negative genetic traits.

00:03:29.530 --> 00:03:31.490
So, they are siblings after all?

00:03:31.490 --> 00:03:34.080
I have to go do maintenance on the machines.

00:03:34.080 --> 00:03:36.580
- Thank you again.
- ﻿Any time.

00:03:36.580 --> 00:03:39.710
- Who cares which I use?!
- It matters!

00:03:39.710 --> 00:03:43.750
- ﻿You go over there, old man!
- What, over here?

00:03:43.750 --> 00:03:49.470
Keep up the pace! One more lap!

00:03:50.090 --> 00:03:54.010
﻿Who'd have guessed that woman was
actually this ship's doctor. What a betrayal!

00:03:54.010 --> 00:03:56.100
So you love Dr. Flaminia, huh?

00:03:56.100 --> 00:03:57.770
Heck no!

00:03:57.770 --> 00:04:00.640
She came to Towasanga on the Crescent Ship,

00:04:00.640 --> 00:04:02.560
so she was a Hermes Foundation spy, right?

00:04:02.940 --> 00:04:06.110
She wasn't a spy exactly.
Don't you agree, Aida?

00:04:06.110 --> 00:04:10.030
More of an investigator driven
by medical curiosity, I'd say.

00:04:10.030 --> 00:04:14.200
Lorucca and Miraji were mad
that she'd tricked them too!

00:04:14.200 --> 00:04:19.040
She says she's having us run to expel
the unwanted bacteria from our bodies.

00:04:19.040 --> 00:04:21.830
At Venus Globe, cleanliness comes first.

00:04:21.830 --> 00:04:24.380
They're stricter about hygiene
than they are about Kuntala.

00:04:24.380 --> 00:04:27.340
That Kuntala stuff is ancient history!

00:04:31.510 --> 00:04:33.260
Let's play squash tomorrow.

00:04:34.220 --> 00:04:37.720
You're holding up pretty well!
That's a former pirate for you!

00:04:37.720 --> 00:04:40.180
A pirate? The heck does that mean?

00:04:40.180 --> 00:04:42.140
Bell, we're playing squash.

00:04:42.140 --> 00:04:43.890
Huh? Oh, sure.

00:04:50.280 --> 00:04:52.070
We're heading out for EVA.

00:04:52.070 --> 00:04:53.910
Roger. Go ahead.

00:04:53.910 --> 00:04:55.870
I'll open the outer door.

00:05:02.290 --> 00:05:04.290
Manny, where is it?

00:05:04.290 --> 00:05:07.250
Lower port side. We need one tank.

00:05:07.250 --> 00:05:08.710
Okay!

00:05:08.710 --> 00:05:11.090
I said these go in the back!

00:05:11.090 --> 00:05:12.720
Oliver!

00:05:12.720 --> 00:05:14.220
I'll help.

00:05:14.220 --> 00:05:15.760
Thanks.

00:05:17.470 --> 00:05:20.010
- I was looking for this.
- ﻿Yeesh!

00:05:22.140 --> 00:05:24.890
- ﻿He laughed!
- He sure did.

00:05:26.480 --> 00:05:27.980
Miraji.

00:05:28.610 --> 00:05:30.780
Push just one of those tanks down to us.

00:05:30.780 --> 00:05:32.900
The Recten will catch it.

00:05:33.900 --> 00:05:35.910
I'd like some repair sheets as well.

00:05:35.910 --> 00:05:37.820
Here you go.

00:05:37.830 --> 00:05:39.370
You know, Miraji...

00:05:39.370 --> 00:05:41.450
You and your people do
a lot of different jobs.

00:05:41.870 --> 00:05:45.250
When you're in a resistance,
you become a jack of all trades.

00:05:45.250 --> 00:05:46.920
Hm. That last tanks goes—

00:05:46.920 --> 00:05:48.420
In back, right?

00:05:48.420 --> 00:05:50.500
Roger that, Miraji.

00:05:53.300 --> 00:05:54.470
Aida.

00:05:55.180 --> 00:05:56.300
Yes?

00:05:56.300 --> 00:05:59.680
is there something going on between
Noredo, Raraiya, and Bell?

00:05:59.680 --> 00:06:05.390
Raraiya and Bell have gotten along
great ever since her memories returned.

00:06:05.390 --> 00:06:07.560
- It won't come loose?
- Yeah.

00:06:07.560 --> 00:06:10.730
This is no good. You'll need to heat it up.

00:06:10.730 --> 00:06:12.030
Really?

00:06:17.990 --> 00:06:20.580
What were those bursts of light over there?

00:06:20.580 --> 00:06:26.870
Cosmic rays. Plasma particles shine
as they impact the ship's beam shield.

00:06:26.870 --> 00:06:29.330
It's similar to an aurora.

00:06:47.520 --> 00:06:49.270
Captain Mask.

00:06:51.320 --> 00:06:53.110
Which of those stars...

00:06:53.780 --> 00:06:56.070
is Luin on?

00:06:56.070 --> 00:06:57.820
I can't tell.

00:07:04.580 --> 00:07:08.000
Happa is dismantling the G-Self in the back.

00:07:08.000 --> 00:07:12.250
What? I'll have him start on routine
inspections for the Rectens today.

00:07:12.250 --> 00:07:15.960
- Adam, is the G-Self in the back?
- ﻿Yeah!

00:07:18.050 --> 00:07:21.260
Mr. Happa, is it giving you trouble?

00:07:21.260 --> 00:07:24.720
I'm able to service it
now, so everything's fine.

00:07:26.850 --> 00:07:29.480
Woah. You fixed this bit that was loose.

00:07:29.480 --> 00:07:33.770
I set the Rayhunton Code back
to its original restricted code.

00:07:33.770 --> 00:07:36.440
I can use this as an escape pod, right?

00:07:36.440 --> 00:07:38.110
The fact that there are code restrictions

00:07:38.110 --> 00:07:43.160
shows that the G-Self is a system that really
wants to keep you guys safe, huh?

00:07:46.120 --> 00:07:49.410
You should be grateful you
had such fine ancestors.

00:08:00.300 --> 00:08:04.260
The parental feelings of those
two people were at work here.

00:08:07.100 --> 00:08:10.730
So, Aida is my sister and
I'm her brother, huh?!

00:08:11.230 --> 00:08:14.900
This is Crescent Ship captain Elle Kind.

00:08:15.440 --> 00:08:18.860
This is an announcement
for our guests from Earth.

00:08:18.860 --> 00:08:23.360
In five minutes, we will be firing
a beam to hit a meteor.

00:08:24.030 --> 00:08:26.120
Fore and starboard.

00:08:29.960 --> 00:08:31.960
Diameter: 100 meters.

00:08:31.960 --> 00:08:34.670
- Distance: 5.2 kilometers.
- Yeah.

00:08:34.670 --> 00:08:36.170
5 kilometers.

00:08:40.380 --> 00:08:42.930
- What precision!
- ﻿I'm impressed.

00:08:42.930 --> 00:08:45.010
What if they fail to hit it,

00:08:45.010 --> 00:08:48.260
or a meteor big enough to get through
the beam barrier comes along?

00:08:48.260 --> 00:08:51.430
- If that happened this ship would—
- Go boom, I'll bet!

00:08:51.440 --> 00:08:53.560
- Right?
- ﻿You've got that right.

00:08:53.560 --> 00:08:55.270
I wanna go home!

00:08:55.270 --> 00:08:56.940
Well, yeah, I can understand, but...

00:08:56.940 --> 00:09:00.530
If you want off the ship,
it would be faster to go there.

00:09:00.530 --> 00:09:02.110
I-Is that...

00:09:02.110 --> 00:09:04.490
Venus Globe?

00:09:05.700 --> 00:09:08.410
Designed in Towasanga,

00:09:08.410 --> 00:09:13.080
that is the Venus Globe, constructed
by the Hermes Foundation.

00:09:17.000 --> 00:09:20.300
The magnetic storms of Venus
are pretty bad but—

00:09:20.300 --> 00:09:22.050
What is it, Chickara?

00:09:22.050 --> 00:09:27.430
The Crescent Ship is currently shifting
to an entry course for the Ocean Ring.

00:09:27.430 --> 00:09:33.520
Honestly, I'd like to test out this
Anti-Minovsky thing the Grod has, Captain Kia.

00:09:33.520 --> 00:09:36.730
We're going to take the Crescent Ship.

00:09:43.030 --> 00:09:47.820
The energy emitted when the
G-Self flew inside this ship

00:09:47.830 --> 00:09:49.950
was trapped inside the ship

00:09:49.950 --> 00:09:54.000
and through that, the engine was activated.

00:09:54.000 --> 00:09:59.130
The excitation of the system caused
a 10% increase in efficiency.

00:09:59.670 --> 00:10:04.130
So, then, was that because
of the shape of this ship?

00:10:04.130 --> 00:10:08.390
But of course. The entire hull of
the ship had a photon reaction.

00:10:08.970 --> 00:10:11.850
It works on the same principal
as the G-Self's reflectors.

00:10:11.850 --> 00:10:13.100
Really?

00:10:13.100 --> 00:10:15.810
So, the Rayhunton Code has
nothing to do with it then?

00:10:15.810 --> 00:10:19.360
Yes. The photon reaction is
an issue of circulation.

00:10:21.320 --> 00:10:23.900
So the form reflects the function.

00:10:23.900 --> 00:10:25.450
Well, of course it does.

00:10:25.450 --> 00:10:27.490
- Oh, I get it!
- Huh'?

00:10:27.490 --> 00:10:32.160
We constructed the YG, the
G-Self using the data we had.

00:10:32.160 --> 00:10:34.540
Once it passed the Dorette Army's checks,

00:10:34.910 --> 00:10:37.580
we never gave a thought
to the theory behind its energy.

00:10:37.580 --> 00:10:41.540
Sneaking the Rayhunton Code into
it was the only thing on our minds.

00:10:41.550 --> 00:10:44.550
- ﻿I see...
- ﻿As for the Megafauna,

00:10:44.550 --> 00:10:49.140
it was put together pretty much exactly
as the Rose of Hermes Blueprints said.

00:10:49.140 --> 00:10:52.510
We don't have a single engineer
who really gets how it works, do we?

00:10:52.850 --> 00:10:54.350
You're kidding me!

00:10:54.350 --> 00:10:56.600
And you people came up
to space in this thing?

00:10:57.560 --> 00:11:02.150
We had records in the history books of the
tech that supported the Universal Century.

00:11:02.150 --> 00:11:03.730
It's technology that brought
about ruin though.

00:11:03.730 --> 00:11:07.900
It's precisely because people were left
behind in space and were in despair

00:11:07.910 --> 00:11:10.570
that Towasanga and that thing were built.

00:11:10.570 --> 00:11:15.200
The Venus Globe is a photon battery
production plant, isn't it?

00:11:15.200 --> 00:11:19.710
No, you should think of the whole
thing as one massive battery.

00:11:19.710 --> 00:11:21.920
We live in the Ocean Ring,

00:11:21.920 --> 00:11:25.760
and want to finish filling the area inside
with a globe of nothing but batteries.

00:11:25.760 --> 00:11:28.010
How large will the globe be?

00:11:28.010 --> 00:11:30.470
About the size of the moon, I imagine.

00:11:30.470 --> 00:11:32.090
The moon?

00:11:32.100 --> 00:11:34.390
Such a vast amount of energy...

00:11:34.390 --> 00:11:35.810
What will you use it for?

00:11:35.810 --> 00:11:38.980
To let humanity live on forever.

00:11:38.980 --> 00:11:43.230
On Earth, we are not allowed to improve on
Ag-Tech, which is science and technology.

00:11:43.230 --> 00:11:46.400
After forcing that taboo on us,
this is awfully selfish of you.

00:11:46.400 --> 00:11:51.360
Humans rendered the Earth uninhabitable
through mass consumption and war.

00:11:51.870 --> 00:11:55.490
That aspect of human nature made
the Ag-Tech taboo necessary.

00:11:55.490 --> 00:12:00.460
In exchange, the foundation has provided you
photon batteries with no questions asked.

00:12:00.460 --> 00:12:04.420
Because you let Capital Tower monopolize
the distribution of energy.

00:12:04.420 --> 00:12:05.710
the people on other continents—

00:12:05.710 --> 00:12:08.170
Don't speak purely from
Amerian sensibilities!

00:12:08.170 --> 00:12:09.420
Don't speak!

00:12:09.420 --> 00:12:11.430
The people's freedom is being infringed!

00:12:11.430 --> 00:12:14.220
Shouldn't people comply
with the rhythm of nature?

00:12:14.220 --> 00:12:16.140
But in Ameria—

00:12:16.140 --> 00:12:19.890
You were taught to think that
way growing up, I see.

00:12:20.730 --> 00:12:22.060
Taught?

00:12:22.730 --> 00:12:24.230
What do you mean I was taught?

00:12:24.230 --> 00:12:27.020
He means it's not something
you sensed on your own.

00:12:27.030 --> 00:12:29.990
Taught. Inputting. Taught.

00:12:29.990 --> 00:12:32.240
it was instilled in me, you mean?

00:12:37.160 --> 00:12:39.330
The Triplet can go back to the lab.

00:12:39.330 --> 00:12:41.830
We'll be coming back in the Crescent Ship.

00:12:47.250 --> 00:12:50.010
So, this information you
got from Towasanga...

00:12:50.010 --> 00:12:51.470
It's reliable, right?

00:12:51.470 --> 00:12:54.430
We're going to find that out.

00:12:54.430 --> 00:12:58.600
You can't trust a thing those
Earth Sphere people say.

00:13:11.280 --> 00:13:12.940
You read me, right?

00:13:12.940 --> 00:13:14.820
Everyone who can hear me,
raise your right hand.

00:13:20.580 --> 00:13:25.250
Very good. Don't move away from
the Arcane, even as a joke.

00:13:25.250 --> 00:13:28.960
Don't go thinking you can return to the
Crescent Ship using your suit's verniers.

00:13:31.960 --> 00:13:34.630
In space, even distant things look close.

00:13:34.630 --> 00:13:38.390
Even if you think you've grasped the
Crescent Ship's size from the numbers,

00:13:38.390 --> 00:13:40.970
that is different from actually seeing it.

00:13:40.970 --> 00:13:43.180
You need to get a real
sense of that difference.

00:13:43.180 --> 00:13:45.270
If you understand what I said,
raise both hands.

00:13:45.270 --> 00:13:48.730
Yeah!

00:13:48.730 --> 00:13:52.770
The colors let you tell left
from right even at a distance.

00:13:52.780 --> 00:13:54.320
She was right.

00:13:54.320 --> 00:13:56.950
There's supposedly a kilometer
between here and there.

00:13:57.490 --> 00:13:59.200
I can't see it.

00:13:59.200 --> 00:14:02.410
When you understand something
through numbers, it's just numbers.

00:14:02.410 --> 00:14:05.120
They're doing routine maintenance
over there, too.

00:14:05.120 --> 00:14:08.540
There's no way it's a kilometer away.

00:14:08.540 --> 00:14:09.960
There is.

00:14:10.630 --> 00:14:12.040
It's getting dim.

00:14:12.050 --> 00:14:14.170
- You should clench your hands.
- Is that right?

00:14:14.170 --> 00:14:16.380
- What's so funny?
- Hey, you're right!

00:14:16.380 --> 00:14:18.130
- ﻿I can hear everyone.
- ﻿Wow!

00:14:18.130 --> 00:14:21.890
- ﻿Our mikes are open?!
- No turning it off. That could get you killed.

00:14:21.890 --> 00:14:23.140
I know that.

00:14:23.520 --> 00:14:27.020
Is what my father taught me wrong?

00:14:27.020 --> 00:14:30.270
Huh? I think, as military
men go, he's a great guy!

00:14:30.560 --> 00:14:35.070
M-My mother the Operations Director
was a little unrefined,

00:14:35.070 --> 00:14:37.110
but she was a fine mother, with
a strong sense of responsibility.

00:14:37.610 --> 00:14:38.570
Yeah.

00:14:38.570 --> 00:14:39.450
We've arrived.

00:14:40.370 --> 00:14:43.080
Stop pulling!

00:14:43.080 --> 00:14:44.740
Jump!

00:14:46.040 --> 00:14:48.710
So which part is this Ocean Ring?

00:14:48.710 --> 00:14:50.870
If you know what you're
looking for, you can see it.

00:14:50.880 --> 00:14:53.960
- ﻿It's just above the Venus Globe.
- Right.

00:14:53.960 --> 00:14:57.760
Since they call it the Ocean Ring,
is there a sea there?

00:14:57.760 --> 00:15:00.340
Something like that.

00:15:00.340 --> 00:15:04.260
That we've gone so far as building something
like that so that we could live here

00:15:04.260 --> 00:15:08.640
is definitive proof of how
precious the Earth is.

00:15:08.640 --> 00:15:14.270
On Earth, there are competing space
fleets feuding over the Capital Tower.

00:15:14.270 --> 00:15:17.280
It's because of increased
economic affluence, I suppose.

00:15:17.280 --> 00:15:19.320
I don't care about your grownup reasons!

00:15:19.740 --> 00:15:22.490
In order to stop the fighting,

00:15:22.490 --> 00:15:26.790
I want to have someone like my sister meet
with the bigwigs of the Hermes Foundation,

00:15:26.790 --> 00:15:31.210
to see this Venus Ring, or Ocean Ring,
or whatever it's called,

00:15:32.330 --> 00:15:36.130
and to find this dream of a sea in space!

00:15:37.130 --> 00:15:38.130
Bellri.

00:15:38.510 --> 00:15:42.890
The current ruler of Venus
Globe, a man named La Gu,

00:15:42.890 --> 00:15:45.390
is very noble.

00:15:45.810 --> 00:15:47.560
I'm glad things have worked out.

00:15:47.560 --> 00:15:50.850
Bell's managed to accept Aida as his sister.

00:15:50.850 --> 00:15:53.770
He's a strong kid. With real resilience.

00:15:53.770 --> 00:15:55.400
What's that? What?

00:15:56.320 --> 00:15:59.940
Captain, they're saying the G-IT
Corps will come out to greet us.

00:15:59.940 --> 00:16:01.530
Agh! Not again!

00:16:01.530 --> 00:16:04.820
- ﻿Is that the image?
- ﻿I don't know of any G-IT Corps.

00:16:04.820 --> 00:16:06.530
- What are they?
- Is this them?

00:16:06.530 --> 00:16:08.410
I don't know those Mobile Suits.

00:16:08.410 --> 00:16:10.410
What do you think's going on here?

00:16:10.410 --> 00:16:12.580
Play back the intelligible parts for me.

00:16:16.000 --> 00:16:18.880
Is that the welcoming party from Venus Globe?

00:16:18.880 --> 00:16:21.380
They look like that legendary Mobile Suit.

00:16:25.720 --> 00:16:27.220
Th-They're here!

00:16:28.390 --> 00:16:31.390
Th-Those are G-type suits, aren't they?

00:16:34.850 --> 00:16:37.310
Look at that pose. Are they
actually here to greet us?

00:16:37.320 --> 00:16:38.860
They sure don't look peaceful.

00:16:44.660 --> 00:16:46.110
They're moving.

00:16:50.950 --> 00:16:53.370
I've confirmed the presence
of Captain Elle Kind.

00:16:53.370 --> 00:16:56.500
I've heard nothing about some G-IT
Corps coming out to welcome us!

00:16:56.500 --> 00:16:59.840
You will release the Crescent Ship
into our possession.

00:17:00.380 --> 00:17:01.590
Where is Bellri?

00:17:01.590 --> 00:17:05.300
Have all of the Earthnoids
aboard move to the Megafauna.

00:17:05.300 --> 00:17:08.760
I only want formal crew
members on this bridge.

00:17:08.760 --> 00:17:11.100
You Earthnoids too.

00:17:11.100 --> 00:17:13.980
It's just a short jump from there
to the Megafauna, I'll bet.

00:17:15.770 --> 00:17:17.190
My prince!

00:17:17.560 --> 00:17:19.480
What is with you people?

00:17:20.280 --> 00:17:22.190
- ﻿﻿Bell!
- Kid!

00:17:23.070 --> 00:17:25.200
- You can't do this.
- ﻿What was that?

00:17:26.070 --> 00:17:27.610
Bell!

00:17:29.580 --> 00:17:30.870
You villains!

00:17:30.870 --> 00:17:33.000
What is the G-IT Corps?

00:17:33.000 --> 00:17:36.210
You certainly haven't come out here
to greet us with La Gu's permission.

00:17:36.210 --> 00:17:39.290
Captain, he gave his name as Kia Mbeki.

00:17:39.670 --> 00:17:41.630
Let him in. I want to see his face.

00:17:43.590 --> 00:17:45.090
I am the XO—

00:17:45.720 --> 00:17:47.090
Woah there.

00:17:47.090 --> 00:17:51.310
If you let Earthnoids in here,
there's no telling what they might do.

00:17:52.680 --> 00:17:54.350
Kia Mbeki?

00:17:54.350 --> 00:17:57.140
Director of Technology Preservation
at the G-IT Laboratory.

00:17:57.150 --> 00:17:59.980
If the Megafauna does anything
besides what we tell it...

00:17:59.980 --> 00:18:02.070
We know!

00:18:02.070 --> 00:18:04.610
There's a woman lacking in charm.

00:18:12.120 --> 00:18:13.830
Here they come!

00:18:14.290 --> 00:18:15.620
Get inside!

00:18:16.580 --> 00:18:17.620
Everyone!

00:18:17.620 --> 00:18:20.000
- Use your verniers!
- ﻿Yeah!

00:18:20.000 --> 00:18:22.670
- ﻿To the hangar!
- Operating verniers.

00:18:26.930 --> 00:18:28.340
There are six enemy machines.

00:18:28.340 --> 00:18:30.390
That big one is worth two
or three by itself...

00:18:33.220 --> 00:18:35.520
Take turns entering the airlock. Huh?

00:18:35.520 --> 00:18:37.060
Huh?

00:18:37.690 --> 00:18:39.310
You don't need to turn on the lights.

00:18:39.310 --> 00:18:42.610
- Why?
- ﻿Do you read me over the contact link?

00:18:42.610 --> 00:18:45.820
If you turn on the red lights,
it'll put them on the alert.

00:18:45.820 --> 00:18:47.080
Oh.

00:18:48.530 --> 00:18:51.780
As per their orders, we can't
make any careless moves now.

00:18:52.370 --> 00:18:55.240
- We just have to stay inside, right?
- That should be right.

00:18:59.500 --> 00:19:01.120
It's open.

00:19:01.130 --> 00:19:02.580
What are they looking at?

00:19:05.590 --> 00:19:08.420
What are you doing? You people—

00:19:08.420 --> 00:19:09.720
Mr. Happa!

00:19:09.720 --> 00:19:11.430
They're planning to steal the G-Self!

00:19:11.430 --> 00:19:13.180
Who?

00:19:13.180 --> 00:19:14.600
He came back!

00:19:14.600 --> 00:19:17.560
Dr. Flaminia! What do you think you're doing?

00:19:17.980 --> 00:19:21.400
The panels and styling
are all Universal Standard!

00:19:21.400 --> 00:19:23.230
Why won't it move for me?!

00:19:23.730 --> 00:19:26.190
This suit was an inheritance from my parents!

00:19:26.190 --> 00:19:28.570
It's not universal.

00:19:28.570 --> 00:19:31.030
It belongs to just me,
my sister, and Raraiya!

00:19:31.320 --> 00:19:35.870
Tools for use in space
must be usable by anyone!

00:19:35.870 --> 00:19:38.000
Well, the G-Self is different!

00:19:38.000 --> 00:19:40.500
That's against the taboo!

00:19:43.670 --> 00:19:45.080
Lieutenant Kerbes!

00:19:45.090 --> 00:19:47.250
- ﻿Bellri, can you see it?
- ﻿What?

00:19:47.260 --> 00:19:49.050
Bellri! What's going on?
- ﻿Mr. Happa!
- Bellri?!

00:19:49.050 --> 00:19:51.470
What's Dr. Flaminia doing?
- The G-Self?!
- Huh?!

00:19:51.470 --> 00:19:54.300
Dr. Flaminia threw Bellri out!

00:19:54.850 --> 00:19:57.010
- It's not working.
- No way.

00:19:57.930 --> 00:19:59.060
Gunda—

00:19:59.430 --> 00:20:02.230
Looks like we won't need
to seize it by force!

00:20:02.230 --> 00:20:04.020
None of you resist!

00:20:04.900 --> 00:20:06.270
What did you say happened to Bell?

00:20:06.520 --> 00:20:08.440
Bell! Is he dead?!

00:20:08.440 --> 00:20:10.440
We haven't gone outside!

00:20:10.450 --> 00:20:13.030
We're abiding by our orders.

00:20:13.030 --> 00:20:14.950
Yeah, I get that.

00:20:14.950 --> 00:20:17.030
But you're those war-loving Earthnoids.

00:20:17.040 --> 00:20:21.160
You take a single step outside, and
I'll have to reduce you to space dust.

00:20:21.160 --> 00:20:24.880
I'm sure war-lovers like you can
imagine how powerful the Grod is.

00:20:27.800 --> 00:20:31.670
I-It's like a laser cannon.

00:20:31.670 --> 00:20:34.970
I'd bet that thing could
blast through a battleship.

00:20:34.970 --> 00:20:40.640
I had always believed the people creating
the photon batteries were peaceful.

00:20:41.020 --> 00:20:43.020
Is Bellri dead?

00:20:43.520 --> 00:20:46.270
- Dr. Flaminia!
- He's not dead.

00:20:46.770 --> 00:20:50.400
Bellri's always working too hard.
He could use the rest.

00:20:50.400 --> 00:20:53.320
Yaan, I understand how you feel now.

00:20:53.320 --> 00:20:55.660
- I'll handle the rest.
- S-Sorry about this.

00:20:55.660 --> 00:20:59.280
I had thought we should take
over this ship first thing...

00:21:00.620 --> 00:21:02.910
He'll wake up after a night's rest.

00:21:02.910 --> 00:21:05.750
It's not like he was given
the full injection.

00:21:05.750 --> 00:21:07.670
You're sure, right?

00:21:15.180 --> 00:21:18.010
But why are so many of you
bundled up together in here?

00:21:22.230 --> 00:21:24.390
- Huh?
- Surveillance cameras?

00:21:24.390 --> 00:21:27.150
They've rounded up all the
dangerous elements here.

00:21:28.610 --> 00:21:30.770
I have something to tell
the crew of the Megafauna.

00:21:30.780 --> 00:21:33.940
We've come out here at the direction
of Towasanga's Hazm Government,

00:21:33.950 --> 00:21:38.160
with orders to deal with you people.

00:21:38.160 --> 00:21:40.070
I want to make you aware of that.

00:21:40.080 --> 00:21:41.830
H-Hold on!

00:21:41.830 --> 00:21:43.330
This is by the will of the Rosario Ten,

00:21:43.330 --> 00:21:46.500
and with the assent of the
President La Gu, right?

00:21:47.380 --> 00:21:48.380
Captain!

00:21:48.750 --> 00:21:51.590
The Rosario Ten and La Gu
have nothing to do with us!

00:21:51.590 --> 00:21:55.090
The G-IT Laboratory received
the contract for this job directly.

00:21:55.090 --> 00:21:57.970
You'll be cursed for this! Cursed!

00:21:57.970 --> 00:22:00.680
The Rosario Ten will get
in the way, you know?

00:22:00.680 --> 00:22:02.390
Some of them sympathize with us.

00:22:02.390 --> 00:22:05.730
Because this plan is
perfect for the G-IT Lab.

00:22:05.730 --> 00:22:07.980
The time has come.

00:24:00.600 --> 00:24:02.930
When the G-IT Corps threaten
me into going out to fight,

00:24:02.930 --> 00:24:05.770
I find myself leaping into a universe
that's completely unfamiliar to me.

00:24:05.770 --> 00:24:09.270
It's because there are giant
battery balls and a frame.

00:24:09.270 --> 00:24:11.860
Trying to fight without
destroying those things...

00:24:11.860 --> 00:24:13.820
Even a god couldn't do it!

00:24:13.820 --> 00:24:17.740
I can't be proud about my battle
because I end up destroying them.

00:24:18.780 --> 00:24:23.040
Next time on Reconguista in G,
Space Inside a Frame.

00:24:23.040 --> 00:24:26.460
You people saying it can't ﻿exist, please, watch.
